    LLM: 'Game: MakaÃ³ (Hungarian Shedding). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "MakaÃ³ (often referred to as 'Mak-Var' in regional contexts) is the most popular shedding card game in Hungary and much of Central Europe. It is the tactical ancestor of games like Uno and Crazy Eights. Using a standard 32-card or 52-card deck, players attempt to discard all their cards while using powerful action cards to penalize opponents. The game's name comes from the requirement to shout 'MakaÃ³!' when one card remains.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to discard all cards from your hand.',
    gameplay: '1. Play a card that matches either the **suit** or the **rank** of the top card on the pile.\n2. If you cannot play, draw one card from the deck.',
    keyRules: [
      "Play a card matching the top card's suit or rank; Ace and Joker are wild.",
      'If you cannot play, draw one card from the deck.',
      "When down to one card you must call 'Makaó'; if an opponent calls first you draw 5.",
      'Action cards: 2 (next draws 2, stackable), 3 (next draws 3, stackable), 4 (next misses a turn, stackable), Jack (call a value), King Spades/Hearts (draw 5 or stack), Joker (reverse direction), Ace (call new suit).',
